<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Huasteca</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Huasteca is a region on the Gulf coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, covering parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veracruz">Veracruz</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-luis-potosi">San Luis Potosí</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamaulipas">Tamaulipas</a>, Hidalgo, Querétaro and Puebla. Named after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huastec-people">Huastec people</a>, its fertile lowlands produced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> and textiles, and from the 15th century much of it paid tribute to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a>. It is also home to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nahuas">Nahua</a>, Otomí and Pame communities.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/huasteca.jpg" alt="Huasteca" width="320" height="172" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: RAXERIOS · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Captura_de_Pantalla_2020-03-11_a_la(s)_8.33.27.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
